  "description": "The award-winning Vitus Zenium - Local criteriums, speedy sportives, weekend club runs or your go-to training bike, the Zenium has you covered.\n\nThe Zenium is designed to offer the perfect blend of comfort and performance for a great all-round riding experience. The compact geometry and slender dropped seat stays increase comfort, and give a balanced ride. The UD carbon fork features a tapered steerer for steering precision and inspiring handling, balancing confidence and control. We’ve built in up to 32mm tyre clearance to give you more choice. The frame is a fine balance of classic tube shapes and modern features, put together in a package that keeps weight to a minimum. Make no mistake, the Zenium wants to go fast! However, the subtle nods to all-day comfort ensure that if you are looking for a carbon road all-rounder, then the Zenium is for you.\n\nThe Zenium CRS Di2 Disc comes fitted with the high-performance Shimano Ultegra R8050 11 speed electronic groupset and Ultegra hydraulic flat mount disc brakes. For performance and reliability, the Ultegra Di2 groupset is hard to beat.\n\nThis model features the all-new Prime Baroudeur Disc Tubeless Ready clincher wheels, with slick new graphics, and a very competitive weight. These are paired with tubeless ready Schwalbe ONE 28mm tyres. The new Vitus Switch axles give you the option to leave the lever handle firmly secured in either wheel or remove it for the extra weight saving and aero gains. The cockpit is built with Vitus’ own 6061 Aluminium aero bar and stem, combined with a Vitus 27.2mm US Carbon layback seatpost and our own tried and tested Vitus road saddle.\n\nLightweight carbon frame & fork\n\nInternal cable routing\n\nShimano Ultegra Di2 R8070\n\nHydraulic disc brakes\n\nPrime Baroudeur wheels\n\nVee Road Runner 700 x 28 tyres",
